think r1 landed and sent (a council loads a sky; the odd fractal gives a tie-free quorum). r2 is the next rung: bind each ballot to the voting seat's settled Kumara identity, mirroring skate_group_signed / commerce_trade_signed. Agent-doable — demo seeds only, no custody crossed.
think Read skate_group_signed.rye for the exact idiom (tag + fixed-field message, Keyring point->key, verify-before-touch, honesty-crux relabel, forged/unknown/cross-group refusals).
think Council ballots vote by seat index (r1's abstraction), so the Keyring maps seat->key and the signed message carries tag, council_id, size, seat, proposal, and the yes/no as one byte. The size is signed too, so a ballot cannot cross a differently-shaped body; vote_signed checks over council.size.
think The honesty crux for a council is flipping yes->no after signing (mirrors the group's candidate relabel) — the signature was over the choice actually made, so it falls BadConsent. Forged (wrong seed), unknown seat, cross-council each refuse; the odd-quorum lone-hand guard carries through r1 (AlreadyVoted, tally unmoved).
obs GREEN first pass; TAME bans + width clean; r1 re-runs GREEN (additive). verify_ballot touches no council, so r3 can re-check a traveled ballot offline.
